  {
    "udt_error_enum_v0": {
      "doc": "Error codes live at 100+ **on purpose**.\\n\\n`claim`, `deposit` and `execute_reclaim` all invoke a token\\ncontract, and a Stellar Asset Contract raises its own `contracterror`\\ncodes in the low single/double digits \\xe2\\x80\\x94 notably `BalanceError = 10`\\n(\"insufficient balance\"). When such a sub-invocation trap surfaces to a\\ncaller that only sees `Error(Contract, #N)`, an SAC code is\\nindistinguishable from a vesting code of the same value: an underfunded\\ncampaign reported `#10`, which the vesting ABI called `NotInitialized`,\\nso a recipient hitting an empty campaign was told \"campaign not\\ninitialized\". Moving the whole enum above every SAC code makes the\\norigin of a numeric code unambiguous.\\n\\nThe mapping from the pre-100 numbering is exactly `new = old + 100`, so\\nold decoders migrate by adding 100. `112` is deliberately left unused:\\nit was `MerkleRootFunded`, removed as dead code (see `set_merkle_root`).",
      "lib": "",
      "name": "Error",
      "cases": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "InvalidProof",
          "value": 101
        },
